legend bottom left
  UC-4 only: RITUAL_READY -> ACTIVE after a successful ritual.
  CORRECTION / EMERGENCY are operating conditions, NOT SeasonPlanStatus values.
  Critical condition = any operational CRITICAL MagicIncident.
  No planning, approval, preparation commands, completion or report subsystem.

  Completeness: all declared fields, constructors and explicit methods of UC-4 types.
  Grey <<UC4 projection>> = shared class/interface: only UC-4 operations/literals; other use cases intentionally excluded.
  Record fields are private final. Canonical constructors are shown; accessors, equals/hashCode/toString are implicit.
  Java-generated enum values/valueOf and compiler-generated helpers are implicit. JDK/Spring internals are not expanded.

  Relations: solid arrow = navigable association / injected dependency; *-- = composition of session snapshots.
  Dashed arrow = use/create dependency; hollow dashed triangle = interface realization.
  UUID-based associations use IDs, NOT direct object-reference fields or cascade-delete ownership.
  PollenService is the only application class accessing PollenTreeClient; no direct database pollen writes.

  Integration limit: services are core-only; UC-4 REST/UI, readiness/rule adapters, execution persistence,
  metric sensors, periodic scheduler and durable outbox delivery are not wired.
  escalateOverdue() is callable, not a running scheduler.
  Local command transaction covers repositories + audit + outbox, not rollback of external Pollen Tree spending.

  Rules: deviation = round4(abs(value-target)/tolerance); >=1 creates an action, >=2 also a CRITICAL incident.
  Metric uniqueness: (source, sourceEventId); correction deduplicationKey is unique.
  One ritual in progress per plan; finish rechecks readiness, participants and required events.
  Audit entries are append-only. Notify by deduplicated transactional outbox; delivery is a future adapter.

endlegend
